WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:06.580
This is chapter three of Learn
Text.js: Text and Styling.

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:13.210
Every cell has a character, a foreground,
a background and a handful of attributes.

3
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.490
You set them with Text props,
and they land in the cells.

4
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.740
When the frame is logged,

5
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:23.180
Text.js compiles each run of
styled cells into a %c CSS span,

6
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.500
so the console shows real
colors, bold and italics.

7
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.260
First, text attributes.

8
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:40.130
Text takes five attributes: bold, dim,
italic, underline and strikethrough.

9
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.370
Nested Text elements become
styled spans inside one line.

10
00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:50.340
Here, acme-web is bold, and
iad1 takes the accent color.

11
00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.340
Next, theme tokens.

12
00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:01.290
Add a status component in app/status.tsx.

13
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:05.210
A deployment is ready,
building, error or queued.

14
00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:08.570
STATUS gives each one a
label and a theme token:

15
00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.690
success, warning, danger and subtle.

16
00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:17.850
A color can also be a hex value, or a
Tailwind palette class like text-emerald-400.

17
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:22.170
Tokens follow the active theme,
so use them for anything semantic.

18
00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:25.130
Status draws a dot and
the label in that color,

19
00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.540
and wrap="nowrap" keeps it on one row.

20
00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.540
Now, a deployment card.

21
00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.250
In the page, import
useAppTheme, and Status,

22
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.290
STATUS and DeployStatus from the new file.

23
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.850
ORDER is the sequence s steps through.

24
00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:48.690
useAppTheme returns the
current theme and cycleTheme.

25
00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:52.850
t cycles the theme, and s
moves to the next status.

26
00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.450
bg-surface raises the
card off the background.

27
00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.540
wrap="truncate-end" ends
a long commit message with

28
00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.450
an ellipsis instead of
wrapping onto a second row.

29
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.410
And the deployment id
takes the status color,

30
00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:09.620
goes italic while building,
and is struck through on error.

31
00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.930
Here's the card, live on the lesson page.

32
00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.530
Click the pad first.

33
00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.330
Press s, and the deployment is building.

34
00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:20.810
The id turns amber and italic.

35
00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:24.410
Again, and it's an error,
struck through in red.

36
00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.890
Then queued, and back to ready.

37
00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.330
Now press t.

38
00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.650
Five themes ship with Text.js.

39
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:37.210
OpenCode Dark, Tokyo Night, Amber CRT,
Geist Light, and back to Geist Dark.

40
00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:42.380
The whole frame repaints in each palette,
because every color in it is a token.

41
00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.370
Quick check.

42
00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:49.420
Why use color="success"
instead of a hex value?

43
00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.410
Theme tokens follow the active theme.

44
00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:59.700
Tokens resolve against the current theme,
so switching themes recolors every token.

45
00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:04.340
What does wrap="truncate-end" do?

46
00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.650
It ends overflowing text with an ellipsis.

47
00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.500
The line stays one row tall.

48
00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:17.290
Next, in chapter four, you'll move
through deployments with the keyboard,

49
00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.450
and add a help overlay
that lists every shortcut.

50
00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.100
See you there.
